    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1247">

                <pb facs="0869" n="753" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg753"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.512/381.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Vice Consul Bevan to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Tampico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-08-01">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 1, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>List referred to in my July 30 was received today. Nine American companies were
                    assessed for 26,500 pesos and 32 Spanish companies for 73,000 pesos. This office
                    referred Colonel Nafarrate to Governor Caballero’s communication<anchor n="102"
                        xml:id="d1247-f1"/> and requested written statement from him advising of
                    Government change of policy regarding forced loans from foreigners since receipt
                    of said letter. There are over 100 American companies in this district, only
                    nine appear on list, none of them big oil companies. If precedent is established
                    and Americans are compelled to pay forced loans remaining ninety per cent will
                    surely be assessed later on, which will result in the closing down of the large
                    majority of American companies operating here. Will advise Department promptly
                    result of my last communication to Nafarrate.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bevan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1247-f1" n="102" xml:id="d1247-f1-content">
                <p>See telegram of June 5, 1914, from Consul Miller, printed under Forced Loans,
                        <ref target="#pg776">p. 776</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
